+ @dstBuffer receives the decompressed bytes, and may change between calls.
+  Its content is overwritten, so it does not need to be stable across calls.
+ @dstSizePtr is both input and output : on input, the capacity of dstBuffer in bytes;
+  on output, the number of bytes written (necessarily <= the input value).
+ @srcBuffer contains (more) compressed data,
+  and may point to the middle of a larger buffer.
+ @srcSizePtr is both input and output : on input, the number of available bytes in srcBuffer;
+  on output, the number of bytes consumed (necessarily <= the input value).
+  The function may not consume all provided input on each call, so always check *srcSizePtr,
+  and present any unconsumed source bytes again on the next call.
+ @dOptPtr is optional : one can provide NULL, in which case all options are set to default.
+ @return : a hint about how many srcSize bytes LZ4F_decompress() expects for next call.
