+           Any amount of input can always be provided; the value is only a performance hint.
+           A value of 0 means the current frame is fully decoded;
+           if *srcSizePtr is less than the provided value,
+           the unconsumed tail is the start of another frame (if any).
+           Any other value is an error code, which can be tested using LZ4F_isError().
+           After an error, dctx is not resumable :
+           LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext() must be called before reusing it.
+  note 1 : on return, *srcSizePtr and *dstSizePtr hold the bytes actually consumed and produced,
+           and dstBuffer content in [0, *dstSizePtr) is valid decompressed data.
+  note 2 : after finishing a frame (return == 0), it's possible to immediately start feeding
